<TEI xmlns="http://www.tei-c.org/ns/1.0" xml:id="KR1d0052-en-12e705c9" type="transl"><teiHeader><fileDesc><titleStmt><title>Li Ji Dissertation</title><editor role="translator">Jeffrey Riegel</editor></titleStmt><publicationStmt><ab>published electronically as part of the TLS project at https://hxwd.org</ab><availability status="2"><ab>This work has been licensed for use in the TLS</ab></availability></publicationStmt><sourceDesc><bibl><title>Li Ji Dissertation</title>University of California, Berkeleley, PhD, 1978：</bibl><ab>Translation of <bibl corresp="#KR1d0052"><title xml:lang="och">禮記(正文)</title></bibl> into <lang xml:lang="en">English</lang>.</ab></sourceDesc></fileDesc><profileDesc><creation resp="#CH">Initially created: <date>2026-05-04T03:13:18.073+09:00</date> by CH</creation></profileDesc></teiHeader><text><body><div><head>Translated parts</head><p xml:id="KR1d0052-start"><seg corresp="#KR1d0052_tls_032-1a.9" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#CH" modified="2026-05-04T17:26:30.819+09:00">2. For this reason, the gentleman guards what is notseen and is apprehensive6 of what is not heard.7</seg><seg corresp="#KR1d0052_tls_032-1a.3" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#CH" modified="2026-05-04T17:25:02.324+09:00">What Heaven mandates is termed the inborn; 3 </seg><seg corresp="#KR1d0052_tls_032-1a.3-h" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#CH" modified="2026-05-04T17:23:34.4+09:00">Chung Yung( The "Application o f the Inner"^ Debates) [^See Additional Notes fo r my rendering of the t i t l e .]</seg><seg corresp="#KR1d0052_tls_032-1a.4" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#CH" modified="2026-05-04T17:25:07.076+09:00">adhering to the inborn is termed the way; 4 </seg><seg corresp="#KR1d0052_tls_032-1a.5" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#CH" modified="2026-05-04T17:25:21.286+09:00">that one cultivate the way is termed the teaching. 5</seg><seg corresp="#KR1d0052_tls_032-1a.6" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#CH" modified="2026-05-04T17:25:31.519+09:00">B. 1. The way </seg><seg corresp="#KR1d0052_tls_032-1a.7" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#CH" modified="2026-05-04T17:46:21.412+09:00">cannot be left for a moment;</seg><seg corresp="#KR1d0052_tls_032-1a.8" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#CH" modified="2026-05-04T17:26:07.581+09:00">i f i t could be l e f t i t wouldnot be the way. </seg><seg corresp="#KR1d0052_tls_032-1a.10" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#CH" modified="2026-05-04T18:24:04.061+09:00">C. 1. There is nothing more vis ib le than the hidden, </seg><seg corresp="#KR1d0052_tls_032-1a.11" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#CH" modified="2026-05-04T17:27:14.137+09:00">nothing more apparent than the minute. </seg><seg corresp="#KR1d0052_tls_032-1a.12" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#CH" modified="2026-05-04T17:43:47.776+09:00">2. Therefore, the gentleman guards his uniqueness. 9</seg></p></div></body></text></TEI>